            <ArticleTitle>Radiology-Pathology Conference: Calcified untreated gastric cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>418-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adenocarcinoma of the stomach represents upwards of 95% of all gastric malignancy. Calcifications in untreated gastric cancer are rare, but typically represent mucin-producing tumor. We report the radiology and pathology of a patient who presented with gastric wall calcifications on CT and a mucin-producing adenocarcinoma at pathologic examination of a gastric biopsy specimen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
